  "hints": [
    "Read tokens left to right. What do you need to remember about the numbers you have seen but not yet used?",
    "Keep a stack of values. A number is pushed. An operator pops two values (careful: the first pop is the RIGHT operand) and pushes the result.",
    "Reduce modulo 1000000007 after every operation, and normalise subtraction with ((a - b) % M + M) % M so negatives never leak out. Products fit in 64-bit because both factors are below the modulus."
  ],
  "editorial": "A postfix expression is exactly the order in which a stack machine wants its input: push each number, and apply each operator to the two topmost values. Because the expression is valid, exactly one value remains.\n\nThe only traps are the operand order for `-` (the value popped first is the right operand) and size: the real result can have thousands of digits, so every step is reduced modulo `p = 10^9 + 7`. Subtraction can go negative, so add `p` before the final `%` in languages whose `%` keeps the sign. Products of two residues are below `10^18`, which fits in a signed 64-bit integer. JavaScript needs `BigInt` for that product.\n\nTime `O(n)`.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n# evaluate a postfix expression modulo 1000000007\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// evaluate a postfix expression modulo 1000000007\n// readLine() returns the next input line (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    // evaluate a postfix expression modulo 1000000007\n    return 0;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        // evaluate a postfix expression modulo 1000000007\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(data[0])\nM = 10**9 + 7\nst = []\nfor tok in data[1:1+n]:\n    if tok in ('+', '-', '*'):\n        b = st.pop()\n        a = st.pop()\n        if tok == '+':\n            st.append((a + b) % M)\n        elif tok == '-':\n            st.append((a - b) % M)\n        else:\n            st.append(a * b % M)\n    else:\n        st.append(int(tok) % M)\nprint(st[-1])\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\nconst toks = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/);\nconst M = 1000000007n;\nconst st = [];\nfor (const tok of toks) {\n  if (tok === '+' || tok === '-' || tok === '*') {\n    const b = st.pop();\n    const a = st.pop();\n    if (tok === '+') st.push((a + b) % M);\n    else if (tok === '-') st.push(((a - b) % M + M) % M);\n    else st.push((a * b) % M);\n  } else {\n    st.push(BigInt(tok) % M);\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(st[st.length - 1].toString());\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        StringTokenizer tk = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        final long M = 1_000_000_007L;\n        long[] st = new long[n + 1];\n        int top = 0;\n        while (tk.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            String s = tk.nextToken();\n            if (s.equals(\"+\") || s.equals(\"-\") || s.equals(\"*\")) {\n                long b = st[--top];\n                long a = st[--top];\n                long r;\n                if (s.equals(\"+\")) r = (a + b) % M;\n                else if (s.equals(\"-\")) r = ((a - b) % M + M) % M;\n                else r = a * b % M;\n                st[top++] = r;\n            } else {\n                st[top++] = Long.parseLong(s) % M;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(st[top - 1]);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    const long long M = 1000000007LL;\n    vector<long long> st;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        string tok;\n        cin >> tok;\n        if (tok == \"+\" || tok == \"-\" || tok == \"*\") {\n            long long b = st.back(); st.pop_back();\n            long long a = st.back(); st.pop_back();\n            long long r;\n            if (tok == \"+\") r = (a + b) % M;\n            else if (tok == \"-\") r = ((a - b) % M + M) % M;\n            else r = a * b % M;\n            st.push_back(r);\n        } else {\n            st.push_back(stoll(tok) % M);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << st.back() << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  }
